  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Le",
      "h2": "Masculine 'The'",
      "body_html": "<p>French nouns are masculine or feminine. <strong>Le</strong> = the (masculine), <strong>la</strong> = the (feminine). 'Le stylo' (m) but 'la regle' (f). Just memorise the gender with the word.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Bag",
      "h2": "In My Bag",
      "body_html": "<p>'Dans mon sac il y a...' = <strong>'In my bag there is...'</strong>. Then list items: un stylo, un livre, une regle. <strong>Un/une</strong> = a/an.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Plural",
      "h2": "More Than One",
      "body_html": "<p>Add <strong>-s</strong> for plural (silent in French speech). <strong>Les</strong> stylos = the pens. Stay aware of singular vs plural.</p>"
    }
  ],
